{
  "version": 3,
  "note": "How a medicine pack is coded, per country — DATA ONLY, so a contributor can add a country without touching code. Each block answers three questions: (1) which number IDENTIFIES the drug ('codes'), (2) which codes are PACKAGING and must be thrown away ('ignored'), (3) how the printed number can be READ when the barcode is a trap ('ocr': patterns + the sample the guide frame shows). 'scan' and 'catalogue' summarise, for the UI: a country with status 'none' is BLOCKED with a dialog that says so, links this file's documentation and offers the manual entry. ITALY is the worked example: the drug number is the AIC, printed as `A` + 9 digits and ALSO carried by a Code 39 of the bollino on many packs — so a barcode can identify the drug, and the catalogue decides (a read the rows do not contain is a serial). The rest of that sticker is packaging: the lot, the pack's progressive number, the DataMatrix that joins them. The catalogue itself is never bundled: the drugs come from a national open-data import ('dataset', scripts/import-medicines.php --country=XX).",
  "updated": "2026-10-28",
  "sources": [
    "https://www.aifa.gov.it/ (Italy: AIC 9 digits, printed as `A` + 9 digits in Code 39, e.g. A040313076; the medicines dataset is open data, not a free REST API)",
    "https://alfacod.it/codice-barre-farmaci-bollino-farmaceutico-datamatrix (the bollino of a pack carries the AIC and the 'numero progressivo della confezione' as two barcodes — Decreto 2 agosto 2001; the DataMatrix added by the Decreto of 30 May 2014 carries both, and the sticker is printed by the Istituto Poligrafico e Zecca dello Stato)",
    "https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharmazentralnummer (Germany: PZN 8 digits = 7 + check, printed in clear text with the prefix PZN AND as Code 39, which does not contain the letters; Austria: 7 digits inside the EAN as 908888zzzzzzP)",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falsified_Medicines_Directive (EU 2019: 2D DataMatrix with product code, serial, expiry, batch and the national reimbursement number if required)",
    "https://www.gs1.org/standards/barcodes/application-identifiers (AI 01 GTIN, 17 expiry, 10 batch, 21 serial, 710 national health reimbursement number)",
    "https://open.fda.gov/apis/drug/ndc/ (United States: NDC Directory, public domain, JSON, updated daily — the only free national catalogue wired here)",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pharmacode (integer 3..131070, read as binary bars, aka Laetus: a PACKAGING code, not a drug identifier)",
    "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_GS1_country_codes (800-839 Italy, 840-849 Spain, 300-379 France, 400-440 Germany, 500-509 UK, 000-139 US)"
  ],
  "countries": {
    "IT": {
      "name_key": "medical.country_it",
      "status": "full",
      "module": "italy",
      "gs1": [
        [
          "800",
          "839"
        ]
      ],
      "codes": [
        {
          "type": "aic",
          "digits": 9,
          "pattern": "^A\\d{9}$",
          "label_key": "medical.code_aic",
          "printed": true
        }
      ],
      "ignored": [
        {
          "type": "pharmacode",
          "pattern": "^\\d{3,6}$",
          "label_key": "medical.code_line",
          "action": "ocr"
        },
        {
          "type": "laetus",
          "pattern": "^[0-9A-Z]{4,8}$",
          "label_key": "medical.code_line",
          "action": "ocr"
        },
        {
          "type": "progressivo",
          "pattern": "^\\d{9,10}$",
          "label_key": "medical.code_progressive",
          "action": "ocr"
        }
      ],
      "ocr": {
        "label_key": "medical.ocr_btn",
        "hint_key": "medical.scan_hint",
        "sample": "A000000000",
        "patterns": [
          "A[ .:-]?\\d{9}"
        ],
        "frame": {
          "width_pct": 78,
          "height_pct": 26
        },
        "name_search": true
      },
      "fmd": true,
      "fmd_national_ai": "710",
      "dataset": {
        "id": "aifa",
        "label_key": "medical.dataset_aifa",
        "url": "https://www.aifa.gov.it/",
        "importer": "scripts/import-medicines.php --country=IT",
        "licence": "CC-BY",
        "open": true
      },
      "source_key": "medical.src_it",
      "scan": {
        "national_code": "both",
        "barcodes": true,
        "ocr": true,
        "fmd": true,
        "supported": true
      },
      "note": "The AIC is printed as A + 9 digits AND, on many packs, carried by a Code 39 of the bollino: both are the drug, and the catalogue proves which (a serial that starts with an A is in no row). Three other things sit on the same sticker and are PACKAGING: the lot (`16G87N`), the pack's progressive number with its check digit (`0140581421`), and the DataMatrix that joins them — none of them names a medicine. A bare 9-digit read is therefore never a drug on its own: the reader may offer the digit runs of a label to the catalogue, which answers no."
    },
